title A Gauge reading of the six-hundred-dollar month -- underdriven rather than wasted
prompt Keaton asked whether two Claude Max 20x plans and one ChatGPT Pro plan at 600 dollars a month are earning their keep, and whether we are creative enough with what we have; he also noted the standing at-his-keys commands remain unrun.
think Measured before answering: git log counts 503 commits in 7 days and 2,323 in 30; day shelves hold 44 to 85 session logs per day; the week's component mix reads tools 112, construction 69, session-logs 63, context 41 against pond 17, caravan 15, glow 11, brushstroke 11.
think Named two leaks with the observation-inference split: idle fleet wall-clock between hand re-arms, and a commit mix where the tree tending itself takes roughly 285 of 503 against roughly 54 in the product rooms.
think Named what this seat cannot measure -- whether any plan reaches its rate ceiling -- and gave the falsifiable week-long test: no rate-limit waits means the second Max plan is headroom rather than throughput.
obs Four doors ranked Lindy-first crux-first: a self-re-arming fleet loop, wide fan-out spent on wide questions, product campaigns in the CION bounded-queue mold, and seat-shaped ladder assignment.
obs Report once, never urge: the standing at-his-keys lines stand unrun and nothing blocks on them except the pier tidy, the badge cure, and the pier publishers.
